{"type":"text","timestamp":1787403280802,"sessionID":"ses_fd678b513ffeV3czuAWe15Pf3p","part":{"id":"prt_0298997d7001soRDxbRSVVHlRK","messageID":"msg_029895af4001Slrtll8o5pBBlS","sessionID":"ses_fd678b513ffeV3czuAWe15Pf3p","type":"text","text":"The helper implementations now satisfy the contract:\n\n- `basename` (lib/utils.js:61) splits on `/`, or `[\\\\/]` when `windows`, strips trailing empty segments, returns the last real segment (or `''`).\n- `escapeLast` (lib/utils.js:36) escapes the last occurrence of `char` at/below `lastIdx`, but when that occurrence is already preceded by `\\` it searches further left instead of double-escaping.\n- `removePrefix` (lib/utils.js:42) defaults `state = {}`, strips a single leading `./`, records `state.prefix = './'`, and leaves `state` untouched otherwise.\n\nVerified against the contract (results above all correct).\n\nNote: the 5 failing tests in `test/match.test.js` are **pre-existing** — they fail identically before my change (confirmed via `git stash`). They concern the broader library (and test #7's line 48 asserts `c.md` matches `*.js`, which is semantically wrong) and are outside the helper scope. My change didn't break the 3 passing tests. The other helpers are untouched and `matchBase` routes through the corrected `basename`.","time":{"start":1787403278295,"end":1787403280797}}}
